# Step 2.1 — hackathons. Run `bun run dev`; VS Code "REST Client" keeps cookies between requests.
# Sign in as an admin first (create one with `bun run admin create`), then as a normal user.
@base = http://localhost:3000
@origin = http://localhost:3000

### Sign in as admin
POST {{base}}/api/auth/sign-in/email
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{ "email": "asha@example.com", "password": "REPLACE_ME" }

### Create (slug derived from the name → "hackfest-2026") → 201
POST {{base}}/api/hackathons
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{ "name": "HackFest 2026!", "description": "Remote, 48 hours.", "minTeamSize": 2, "maxTeamSize": 4 }

### Same slug again → 409 SLUG_TAKEN
POST {{base}}/api/hackathons
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{ "name": "HackFest 2026", "minTeamSize": 2, "maxTeamSize": 4 }

### Explicit slug → 201
POST {{base}}/api/hackathons
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{ "name": "Winter Build", "slug": "winter-build-26", "minTeamSize": 1, "maxTeamSize": 5 }

### Invalid: min > max, max 11, unknown field → 400 with details per field
POST {{base}}/api/hackathons
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{ "name": "Bad", "minTeamSize": 5, "maxTeamSize": 11, "deadline": "tomorrow" }

### List (newest first)
GET {{base}}/api/hackathons

### Detail by slug
GET {{base}}/api/hackathons/hackfest-2026

### Detail by unknown slug → 404 HACKATHON_NOT_FOUND
GET {{base}}/api/hackathons/no-such-hackathon

### Sign in as a normal user → POST gives 403, GETs still work
POST {{base}}/api/auth/sign-in/email
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{ "email": "pat@example.com", "password": "REPLACE_ME" }
